FINAL WORK RECORD (project completed, November 2026)
Role: frontend and user experience.

- Built the React and TypeScript screens: landing page, sign-in and sign-up
  dialog, student dashboard (Hero Portal), and the mission screen with the
  question panel, health bars, timer and result strip.
- Parent and teacher dashboards: the linked-student list, the student report
  view and its single-series SVG charts (practice per day, accuracy over time,
  mastery by topic), badges and observations.
- The camera consent screen, the camera toggle and the calm "camera
  unavailable" message, designed so declining gives an identical game.
- The visual side of the character effects: character portraits with the
  villain GIFs, the CSS/SVG effects layer (web shots, pumpkin bombs, tentacles,
  illusions, tail sweeps, shock rings), the weakened and defeated states, and
  the reduced-motion versions.
- Sound and motion controls that persist across questions and missions.
- Responsive layout, loading and error states, and frontend tests with Vitest
  and React Testing Library (consent flow, dashboards, effects limits).
- The README screenshots and the gameplay recording.

Changes from the plan: written in TypeScript rather than JavaScript, and game
state moved from the browser to the server, so the frontend now displays
results instead of computing them.
